  "format": "tikz",
  "fig_idx": 0,
  "fig_no": 3,
  "caption": "\\textit{Outline of the proof of \\cref{thm:main}.} \n        The proof of \\cref{thm:main} follows a structure analogous to the proof of the sample complexity of PIU learning (\\cref{thm:sampleComplexity}): \n        we construct a sequence of instances of \\pERM{} and output the intersection of all the (approximate) solutions $H_1,H_2,\\dots$ to the instances created.\n        To approximately solve each instance created, we use an approximation algorithm for \\pERM{} (constructed in \\cref{thm:constReg}).\n        This is the main new technical ingredient in the proof of \\cref{thm:main} compared to \\cref{thm:sampleComplexity}.\n        "
 },
